&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;At New Era, you&#39;ll join a team-oriented culture that prioritizes your personal and professional development. Work alongside industry-certified experts, access continuous training, and enjoy competitive benefits. Guided by our core attributes — putting people first, embracing continuous learning, and thriving through collaboration and inclusion — we nurture our people to deliver exceptional customer service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;If you want to make an impact in a supportive, growth-oriented environment, New Era is the place for you. Apply today and help us shape the future of work—together&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Contractor/C2C&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duration:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;6+ months&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Arrangement:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Primarily Remote&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Occasional travel to Philadelphia, PA, as required&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a seasoned&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance &amp;amp; Operations (D365 F&amp;amp;O) Functional Lead&lt;/strong&gt; with deep, hands-on expertise across Finance and Supply Chain Management for an immediate contract engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will bring strong functional knowledge of D365 F&amp;amp;O, including system configuration, financial operations, month-end close, cash application, collections, and related business processes. In addition to functional leadership, this role requires the ability to write or modify code, troubleshoot technical issues, and develop custom modifications to address complex business requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will work closely with business stakeholders, finance teams, supply chain users, and technical teams to analyze requirements, configure the system, resolve functional and technical issues, and deliver effective D365 F&amp;amp;O solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a primarily remote engagement requiring availability during US East Coast business hours. Candidates must be based in the United States, possess excellent English communication skills, and be willing to travel to Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, occasionally when required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;1. D365 F&amp;amp;O Functional Leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead functional activities across Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance and Supply Chain Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather, analyze, and document business requirements from finance, accounting, collections, and supply chain stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business requirements into functional specifications, solution designs, and system configurations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct fit-gap analysis and recommend standard D365 F&amp;amp;O functionality or custom solutions based on business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead functional workshops, requirements discussions, solution walkthroughs, and stakeholder meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide functional guidance to business users and technical teams throughout implementation and enhancement activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure system configurations align with business processes, financial controls, and operational requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;2. Finance and Accounting&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and support core D365 F&amp;amp;O financial modules, including General Ledger, Accounts Receivable, Accounts Payable, and Cash and Bank Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support financial dimensions, account structures, posting profiles, journals, financial calendars, and related configurations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and troubleshoot month-end and year-end closing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support financial reconciliations, transaction postings, period-end adjustments, and financial reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and support customer payment processing, cash application, payment matching, and related reconciliation activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support collections processes, overdue receivables management, customer balances, and collection prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot financial transaction errors, posting issues, and discrepancies between subledgers and the General Ledger.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with financial process improvements, automation opportunities, and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;3. Cash Application and Collections&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and improve cash application processes, including customer payment processing, remittance matching, and payment reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and troubleshoot relevant D365 F&amp;amp;O functionality supporting customer payments and cash application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Accounts Receivable teams to resolve unapplied cash, payment discrepancies, and customer account issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support collections workflows, collection letters, customer aging, credit and collections processes, and outstanding receivables management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate issues involving customer transactions, payment settlements, deductions, and account balances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to streamline cash application and collections through standard functionality, configuration, or custom modifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;4. Supply Chain Management&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide functional expertise across relevant D365 F&amp;amp;O Supply Chain Management processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and support procurement, inventory management, product information, order processing, and related supply chain workflows as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze business processes and identify configuration gaps, process inefficiencies, and system issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot integration and transaction issues affecting finance and supply chain operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure appropriate integration between supply chain transactions and financial postings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with finance and operational stakeholders to validate end-to-end business processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support system enhancements and process optimization across finance and supply chain functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;5. System Configuration and Functional Setups&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform hands-on D365 F&amp;amp;O configuration and maintain relevant system parameters, master data settings, tables, and related functional setups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure modules and business processes based on approved requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand D365 F&amp;amp;O data structures, table relationships, transaction flows, and dependencies between modules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze existing configurations and identify root causes of functional issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document configuration changes, dependencies, and functional design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate configuration changes through functional testing and regression testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;6. Technical Modifications and Custom Development&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write, modify, and troubleshoot code to support D365 F&amp;amp;O customizations and business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with technical teams to design and implement custom modifications where standard functionality does not meet business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate the ability to understand existing code, identify defects, and implement appropriate fixes or enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with X++ and relevant D365 F&amp;amp;O development components, including extensions, classes, tables, and business logic, as applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze technical issues affecting financial and supply chain transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support integrations, data entities, custom business logic, and related technical components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform technical validation and testing to ensure custom modifications function correctly and do not disrupt existing business processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow Microsoft development and extensibility best practices when implementing custom solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;7. Testing, Troubleshooting, and Production Support&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute functional test scenarios and support system integration testing (SIT) and user acceptance testing (UAT).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate end-to-end financial and supply chain processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve application defects, configuration issues, and transaction errors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform root cause analysis and recommend permanent corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support production incidents, system enhancements, and business-critical issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate defect resolution with technical teams, business users, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain documentation for test cases, defects, resolutions, and system changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;8. Stakeholder Communication and Documentation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a functional lead and primary point of contact for assigned D365 F&amp;amp;O workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate technical and functional concepts clearly to business and IT stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare functional specifications, configuration documentation, process flows, test scenarios, and implementation notes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular updates on project progress, risks, dependencies, and outstanding issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate discussions between finance, supply chain, technical teams, and business leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear documentation of decisions, requirements, customizations, and completed deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Skills and Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive hands-on experience with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance &amp;amp; Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong functional expertise in D365 F&amp;amp;O Finance and Supply Chain Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of financial setups, transaction processing, and system configuration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience supporting month-end close and financial reconciliation processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience with cash application, Accounts Receivable, and collections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of D365 F&amp;amp;O tables, data structures, relationships, and transaction flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write, modify, debug, or troubleshoot code and support custom modifications in D365 F&amp;amp;O.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of X++ and D365 F&amp;amp;O development concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with functional specifications, fit-gap analysis, testing, and production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written English communication skills, with the ability to lead stakeholder discussions independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently in a fast-paced contract environment and manage competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be based in the United States and available to work during US East Coast business hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to travel to Philadelphia, PA, occasionally as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
