&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;SecureBlu by New Era Technology is looking for a hands-on DevSecOps Architect specializing in Software Supply Chain Security to help secure software build and release pipelines for our client, Commvault.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have strong experience securing CI/CD pipelines, managing Software Bills of Materials (SBOMs), implementing artifact signing and provenance verification, and securing Kubernetes environments. This role focuses on hands-on implementation of security controls across the software development lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and implement software supply chain security controls across build and release pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Secure GitHub and GitLab environments, including branch protection, signed commits, access controls, and provenance attestation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Implement SBOM generation, validation, and distribution using Syft, CycloneDX, or SPDX.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Integrate dependency scanning and vulnerability management into CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Implement artifact signing and verification using Sigstore, Cosign, or in-toto.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and enforce security-as-code and policy-as-code controls using tools such as Open Policy Agent (OPA), Kyverno, or Conftest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Secure Kubernetes-based build and deployment environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conduct threat modeling for CI/CD pipelines, infrastructure, and AI-assisted development workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assess risks associated with open-source dependencies, AI-generated code, and AI coding assistants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Align security practices with SLSA, NIST SSDF, and NIST SP 800-218.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop security documentation, reference architectures, runbooks, and audit evidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with security, engineering, platform, and compliance teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5–8 years of experience in DevSecOps, application security, or platform engineering, with direct ownership of CI/CD security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong hands-on experience with GitHub Actions, GitLab pipelines, and enterprise-scale repository administration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience generating and managing SBOMs using SPDX or CycloneDX.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of SLSA, NIST SSDF, and NIST SP 800-218.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with artifact signing, provenance, and verification tools such as Sigstore, Cosign, or in-toto.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on Kubernetes security experience, including admission control, network policies, and workload hardening.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with policy-as-code tools such as OPA, Kyverno, or Conftest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understanding of threat modeling methodologies such as STRIDE or attack trees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scripting proficiency in Python, Bash, or Go.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with Docker, OCI images, container registries, and container security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
