&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The primary role of an Experienced Life Safety Service Technician is to assist the Service Manager with the troubleshooting, repair, and maintenance of low voltage systems within a facility. Low voltage systems include fire alarm, video surveillance, door access, AV, audio, paging, intercom, nurse call and network. In this field service role, technicians are also provided opportunities to gain experience in design, estimating, engineering, and sales within the company. This individual will bridge the gap between people and technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRIMARY DUTIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service, Inspecting, testing, and maintaining of low voltage systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot, adjust, calibrate, align, and modify circuitry, components, and programming.&amp;nbsp; Records effects on system performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates attention to detail, accuracy, thoroughness, and dependability by following instructions and being an active listener&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapts well to changing circumstances or conditions in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pursues career development opportunities such as training and certification courses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Always maintains a professional attitude and appearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeps a clean and organized work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adheres to all NEW ERA policies regarding dress code, safety, attendance, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties may occur at your managers discretion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some Engineering for Nurse Call&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPETENCY:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior Access Control, CCTV, Security Alarm, Intercom, and Audio &amp;nbsp;experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Obtain Avixa CTS, NICET, or other industry certifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient system programming experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient use of MS Windows PC and MS Office applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with RTA software and acoustic measurements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must communicate clearly and professionally, verbally and written&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable transportation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with basic hand tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift and carry up to 50 pounds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stoop, balance, stand, walk, sit and climb and/or work on a ladder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED EDUCATION &amp;amp; EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;: &lt;/strong&gt;Associate Electronics degree (or minimum 5 years of experience) in systems installation, service, programming, and commissioning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PHYSICAL DEMANDS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stand on a concrete floor for long periods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift and/or move equipment at least 60 pounds on a repetitive basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to lift equipment and construction supplies from floor height to overhead while loading/unloading trucks or preparing equipment for installations, service calls, and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to climb and work (stack, adjust, and repair) at heights in excess of 25&#39; before/during installations and job sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stand, walk, climb, sit and use hands and fingers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reaching, grasping and carrying activities are also required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Although most work is performed inside, occasional outside activities are subject to seasonal temperature fluctuations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have a clean driving record and valid / current driver’s license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive a company van to client sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;To perform the job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.&amp;nbsp; The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.&amp;nbsp; Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EXPECTED HOURS OF WORK:&lt;/strong&gt; 7:00 am – 4:00 pm Monday - Friday&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRAVEL: &lt;/strong&gt;Local travel to various client locations. No expected overnight travel.&lt;/p&gt;
