&lt;li&gt;Write clean, readable, and maintainable code with team guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews and learn best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help troubleshoot and fix bugs or application issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with developers, QA, and product team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in Agile ceremonies such as daily standups and sprint planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;(or equivalent internship / project experience)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0–5 years of software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Academic, internship, or professional experience with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Java&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Angular and/or React&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web application development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HTML, CSS, and JavaScript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RESTful APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work onsite in Indianapolis 2 days per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong desire to learn and grow as a developer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have (Not Required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
