&lt;p&gt;Successful candidate must possess:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience in project coordination, project administration, procurement, vendor management, or a similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting technology, workplace technology, infrastructure, or operational projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound understanding of procurement processes, including PR and PO management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with vendors, suppliers, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and the ability to effectively manage project documentation and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and relationship-building skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence working independently while managing competing deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, Word, and PowerPoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with procurement platforms such as SAP Ariba or similar systems is highly regarded.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, solutions-focused approach with a commitment to delivering quality outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
