&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LANGUAGE SKILLS:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to read, understand, and interpret job-related documents, instructions, policies, and communications in English. Ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing, with employees, customers, vendors, and other business partners, as applicable to the position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WORK ENVIRONMENT: &lt;/strong&gt;Work is conducted in shop, on construction sites, in finished spaces, and outdoors as required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EXPECTED HOURS OF WORK:&lt;/strong&gt; typical work hours are 7:00am to 3:30 pm however, other shifts including weekends and overtime are often required to meet deadlines and accommodate client needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRAVEL: &lt;/strong&gt;Out of town and overnight travel to clients’ site may be required. Overnight travel expectations is up to 15%.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PHYSICAL DEMANDS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To perform the job&#39;s essential functions, the Associate must be able to stand on a concrete floor for extended periods and lift and/or move equipment at least 60 pounds on a repetitive basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The candidate must be able to lift equipment and construction supplies from floor height to overhead while loading/unloading trucks or preparing equipment for installations, service calls, and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidate must climb and work (stack, adjust, and repair) at heights over 25&#39; before/ during installations and job sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate is required to stand, walk, climb, sit, and use hands and fingers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reaching, grasping, and carrying activities are also required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Although most work is performed inside, occasional outside activities are subject to seasonal temperature fluctuations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
