&lt;p&gt;As a Service Delivery Specialist, you&#39;ll provide remote support for audiovisual and video conferencing systems, manage service requests, coordinate technicians and vendors, and ensure issues are resolved quickly while delivering excellent customer service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following include but may not be limited to the responsibilities of the Service Delivery Specialist:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary contact for clients and vendors regarding service, support, and warranty-related issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide remote troubleshooting and support for audiovisual and video conferencing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and track service requests through the ticketing system, ensuring timely resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate technicians, vendors, and repair resources to deliver efficient service outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process service orders, purchase orders, warranty claims, RMAs, and related documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain service contracts, records, and equipment documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with inventory management and identify potential sales opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver exceptional customer service while ensuring compliance with company processes and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
