&lt;p&gt;New Era has an exciting opportunity for a &lt;strong&gt;Solution Executive, Managed Services&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Solutio&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ns Organization. This individual serves as a senior sales overlay to the field, acting as a subject matter expert and trusted advisor for New Era&#39;s IT Managed Services portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The primary responsibility of the Solution Executive, Managed Services role is to drive recurring revenue growth across New Era&#39;s Managed Services offerings while enabling the field organization to effectively position, qualify, and sell outcome-based managed service solutions. This role partners closely with Account Managers, Sales Directors, Solution Architects, Service Delivery leaders, and strategic technology partners to accelerate managed services adoption and strengthen long-term customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Solution Executive, Managed Services helps customers align operational, financial, and technology objectives with managed service strategies that improve service levels, reduce complexity, increase operational efficiency, and support business transformation initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;***Ideal candidate would reside in the Eastern or Central Time Zone.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRIMARY DUTIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor to clients by understanding business priorities, operational challenges, current IT operating model, technology roadmap, support requirements, and long-term transformation goals, then aligning those needs to New Era’s Managed Services portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Executives and Sales Directors early in the sales cycle to identify, qualify, and advance managed services opportunities across strategic accounts, including Stage 2/3 opportunities, account planning discussions, and top pursuit reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a structured managed services discovery process that identifies customer pain, business risk, decision process, economic buyer, technical champion, current internal or third-party delivery model, competitive alternatives, and the customer’s readiness for operational change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive recurring revenue growth by increasing managed services attach across New Era’s broader solution stack, including cloud, cybersecurity, collaboration/CX, networking, infrastructure, Microsoft/CSP, endpoint, data center, lifecycle services, observability, and professional services.&lt;/li&gt;
