&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role: Senior Network Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Permanent&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Hyderabad / Bangalore (Work from office)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRIMARY DUTIES include but not limited to:&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Implementation Triage &amp;amp; Technical Escalation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the lead escalation point for complex deployment issues during the Cisco‑to‑Fortinet/Juniper migration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot advanced problems involving Fortinet firewalls, Juniper switches, Juniper access points, and legacy Cisco devices during cutovers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support field technicians and implementation teams with real‑time guidance, root‑cause analysis, and corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change Control &amp;amp; Governance (ServiceNow)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full lifecycle of network‑related change controls within ServiceNow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and review change requests with a focus on accuracy, risk mitigation, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high standards of operational discipline and audit readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network Engineering &amp;amp; Migration Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead configuration, deployment, and optimization of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortinet firewalls (policies, VPNs, SD‑WAN, HA, segmentation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juniper switches (EX/QFX series, VLANs, routing, security policies).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juniper access points and wireless controllers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee migration activities including device staging, configuration validation, cutover support, and post‑deployment tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent application of templates, standards, and best practices across all branch refresh activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
